ImmunoTargetNet third-party notices

This release is the code accompanying the manuscript "ImmunoTargetNet: A Multimodal
Multi-Omics Framework for Immune-Related Target Prioritisation in Psoriasis". The MIT
licence above covers the source in this repository. The external resources listed below
keep their own terms, and none of their data is bundled here beyond the derived tables
described in each entry.

Virtual screening and annotation resources
------------------------------------------
Open Targets Platform
  Used for: interaction edges, pathway membership and tractability annotations of the
  keystone evidence layer, read through the public GraphQL API.
  Licence: platform data is released under CC0 1.0; the contributing sources named in each
  edge's sourceDatabase field keep their own terms.
  Source: https://platform.opentargets.org
  API: https://api.platform.opentargets.org/api/v4/graphql

STRING
  Used for: the protein association network behind the interaction edges. The snapshot
  records the originating database of every edge, and STRING scores are the edge weights.
  Licence: STRING data is released under CC BY 4.0; academic use is free.
  Source: https://string-db.org

Molecular Signatures Database (MSigDB)
  Used for: the immune gene-set collections from which the twelve programmes of Sec. 2.4
  are assembled (C5 GO biological process, C2 Reactome, H hallmark), release 2023.2.Hs.
  Licence: MSigDB terms of use; the full corpus requires registration, the three
  collections used here are freely downloadable.
  Source: https://www.gsea-msigdb.org/gsea/msigdb/

Gene expression omnibus series
------------------------------
Eight expression cohorts (GSE53552, GSE30999, GSE182740, GSE69967, GSE85034, GSE201827,
GSE212836, GSE55201), three single-cell resources (GSE254707, GSE176509, GSE173706) and
three spatial resources (GSE206391, GSE310145, GSE299256) are public GEO series. They are
not redistributed here; only their accessions, contrast assignment and reported sample
counts are recorded. Each series keeps the terms its submitters set.
  Source: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/

LINCS L1000 and the Connectivity Map
  Used as the intended source of the compound perturbation reference behind the
  perturbation-consistency term. The resource is not redistributed and the deposited
  signatures are not reachable without registration, so the perturbation-reversal index in
  this release is part of the declared construct rather than a read of that resource.
  Source: https://clue.io

DepMap
  Used as the intended source of the genome-wide loss-of-function dependency map behind
  the perturbation evidence layer. The portal was reachable during preparation and no
  dependency table is bundled.
  Source: https://depmap.org/portal/

